"tutorial.inputModes" = "Choose how much you want to record:\n\n• %1$@ records everything: slope, miss angle and miss reasons.\n• %2$@ records distance, “putt for” (birdie, par, …) and holed or not holed. Little data goes into the statistics in this mode.\n• In %3$@ you can add fields as you like and change how detailed they are.\n\nYour first round is played in %1$@.";
"tutorial.startRound" = "All set! Tap %@ to begin.";
"tutorial.distance" = "Enter the distance from the putt to the hole here. The preset number can be changed in Settings. When the number in the field is black, the entry is saved and you can simply type a new number WITHOUT deleting the old one first. NOTE: to confirm a gray number, you always have to press %@.";
"tutorial.pace" = "Tip: not sure how far a meter is? Pace off a known length and either adjust your stride so one step is a meter, or simply know how far your step is and convert. Usually, though, a slightly longer step is about a meter.";
"tutorial.pace.imperial" = "Tip: not sure how far 3 feet is? Pace off a known length and either adjust your stride so one step is a yard (3 feet), or simply know how far your step is and convert. Usually, though, a slightly longer step is about a yard.";
"tutorial.puttFor" = "Choose here, under “putt for” (birdie, par, …), which score you are putting for. Don't forget this one – it can cause confusion later.";
"tutorial.slope" = "Tap the square that matches the slope of your putt. The putt set here runs 3%% downhill and breaks 2%% from left to right. Try to find your own slope. The straight putt is in the center, at 0. Custom mode has other ways of entering it too, and there are games to improve your green reading.";
"tutorial.missAngle" = "Missed? Tap where the ball stopped in relation to the hole. The slider around the hole sets the exact angle, and the distance left is entered with the next putt. Tap the center if you holed the putt. If it lipped out, you can even tap the lip. For putts like that, though, it's better to mark where the ball would have finished if it hadn't caught the lip.";
"tutorial.missReasons" = "If you know why the putt missed, mark it here. You don't have to, but you can.";
"tutorial.record" = "Tap %1$@ once you've filled in the fields above and entered a result. If the ball is only inches from the hole, skip the whole entry and just press %2$@: the putt is counted from %3$@ and as holed. As soon as the putt is done, we jump automatically to the next putt or the next hole.";
"tutorial.tryRest" = "Now it's your turn: enter the rest of this hole yourself. The next putt starts where the ball stopped, and the preset distance is %@.";
"tutorial.pickUp" = "If you pick up your ball, you can enter it with this symbol. You decide whether to enter a score, and which one.";
"tutorial.holePicker" = "Tap the hole number at the top left to jump to any other hole.";
"tutorial.navArrows" = "Use the arrows to move back and forth between holes.";
"tutorial.puttChips" = "Up here you see every putt of the hole you are on. If there are several, tap one to look at it or change it.";
"tutorial.endRound" = "Tap %@ at the top right to finish the round. The trash can deletes all putts of a hole. You can't break anything – so be sure to try every button, because wherever it matters, Puttor asks you again anyway.";
"tutorial.editLater" = "Even after the round you can still edit your putts and change entries: open the round under “Recent Rounds” and tap “%@” on the hole.";
"tutorial.settings" = "In Settings you choose units, language and the distance a putt starts with, set up the fields of Custom mode and much more.";
"tutorial.finish" = "That's it! Try everything out – and turn your phone sideways too: landscape brings extra functions and layouts. Enjoy your round!";
"settings.tutorial.replay" = "Show the tutorial again";
"settings.tutorial.replay.desc" = "Walks you through your next round";
"settings.tutorial.pending" = "Starts with your next round";
